             PHYS-A1.8: Use a variety of instruments to measure different quantities.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                  \u003c/td>\n                \n                  \u003ctd style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 8px; vertical-align: top; min-height: 280px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;\">\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A1.9: Assess the suitability of instruments on the basis of sensitivity, accuracy and range.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A1.10: Apply the formula for density: ρ = m / V.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #ffe4e6; border: 1px solid #f43f5e; font-weight: bold;\">\n                        SWT 1\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                  \u003c/td>\n                \n              \u003c/tr>\n            \u003c/tbody>\n          \u003c/table>\n        \u003c/div>\n      \n        \u003cdiv style=\"page-break-before: always; margin-top: 36px;\">\n          \u003cdiv style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px;\">\n            \u003ch2 style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.2px;\">\n              Block 2: CHRISTMAS TERM (Weeks 7 - 12)\n            \u003c/h2>\n            \u003cspan style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold; padding: 2px 8px; background: #f1f5f9; border-radius: 4px;\">\n              6 Weeks\n            \u003c/span>\n          \u003c/div>\n\n          \u003ctable style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 2px solid #000; margin-bottom: 24px; table-layout: fixed;\">\n            \u003cthead>\n              \u003ctr>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; text-align: center; background-color: #fff; width: 16%;\">\n                    WEEK 7\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; text-align: center; background-color: #fff; width: 16%;\">\n                    WEEK 8\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; text-align: center; background-color: #fff; width: 16%;\">\n                    WEEK 9\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; text-align: center; background-color: #fff; width: 16%;\">\n                    WEEK 10\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; text-align: center; background-color: #fff; width: 16%;\">\n                    WEEK 11\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; text-align: center; background-color: #fff; width: 16%;\">\n                    WEEK 12\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n              \u003c/tr>\n              \u003ctr>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 8px 4px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; background-color: #fff;\">\n                    26/10/26 - 30/10/26\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 8px 4px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; background-color: #fff;\">\n                    02/11/26 - 06/11/26\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 8px 4px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; background-color: #fff;\">\n                    09/11/26 - 13/11/26\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 8px 4px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; background-color: #fff;\">\n                    16/11/26 - 20/11/26\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 8px 4px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; background-color: #fff;\">\n                    23/11/26 - 27/11/26\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n                  \u003cth style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 8px 4px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; background-color: #fff;\">\n                    30/11/26 - 04/12/26\n                  \u003c/th>\n                \n              \u003c/tr>\n            \u003c/thead>\n            \u003ctbody>\n              \u003ctr>\n                \n                  \u003ctd style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 8px; vertical-align: top; min-height: 280px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;\">\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A2.1: Distinguish between scalars and vectors and give examples of each.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A2.2: Use scale diagrams to find the resultant of two vectors.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                  \u003c/td>\n                \n                  \u003ctd style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 8px; vertical-align: top; min-height: 280px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;\">\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A2.3: Calculate the resultant of vectors which are parallel, anti-parallel and perpendicular.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A2.4: Explain that a single vector is equivalent to two other vectors at right angles.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                  \u003c/td>\n                \n                  \u003ctd style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 8px; vertical-align: top; min-height: 280px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;\">\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.1: Explain the effects of forces.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.2: Identify types of forces.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.3: Determine the weight of objects using W = mg.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                  \u003c/td>\n                \n                  \u003ctd style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 8px; vertical-align: top; min-height: 280px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;\">\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.4: Show how derived quantities and their related units are produced.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.5: Recall the special names given to the units for some derived quantities (e.g., kg m s⁻² = N, N m⁻² = Pa, J = N m).\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                  \u003c/td>\n                \n                  \u003ctd style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 8px; vertical-align: top; min-height: 280px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;\">\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.6: Express derived units using index notation.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.7: Identify situations in which the application of a force will result in a turning effect.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                  \u003c/td>\n                \n                  \u003ctd style=\"border: 2px solid #000; padding: 10px 8px; vertical-align: top; min-height: 280px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;\">\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #f8fafc;\">\n                        PHYS-A3.8: Define the moment of a force: T = F × d.\n                      \u003c/div>\n                    \n                      \u003cdiv style=\"margin-bottom: 8px; padding: 4px 6px; background-color: #ffe4e6; border: 1px solid #f43f5e; font-weight: bold;\">\n                        SWT 2\n                      \u003c/div>\n         